# The same works, asked for a rate rather than a pile.
#
# A total can be met by a warehouse: build storage, let it fill for fifty
# thousand ticks, and ship it all at the end. A sustained rate cannot, which
# makes it a question about the *plant* rather than about the buffer in front
# of it -- and it is the order that punishes a player for buying the bottleneck
# that is not binding.

scenario Steady Gears {
    plant   p1-gears.factory
    brief   Twenty gears every hundred ticks, held for the last twenty thousand.

    budget  1400

    cost process 120 each
    cost link    60  per vehicle
    cost storage 40  per 1000 capacity
    cost source  200 each
    cost sink    80  each
    cost wire    5   each

    order deliver 8000 Gear by 40000
    order sustain 20 Gear per 100 ticks from 40000 to 60000
}
